'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  test-vo-s059-xoro-zero-seed.spin2
''   Purpose....  VO-S059: what do successive ??x return when x starts at
''                0, and what is x afterwards?  (Spin2 ?? against the PASM
''                XORO32 instruction, with non-zero seeds as controls)
''   Manual.....  P2 Knowledge Base
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Oct 2026
''   Updated....  Oct 2026
''
'' ===========================================================================

{ WHAT IS DECIDED  (register VO-S059; close-out study step 8)

  No ingested source gives the recurrence, the period or the zero case of
  the P2 xoroshiro32+ iteration.  The sources say only:
    - the instruction: "XORO32 D - Iterate D with xoroshiro32+ PRNG algorithm
      and put PRNG result into next instruction's S"
      (p2-datasheet-text.txt:1557; the instruction CSV row 413; the PASM2
      manual table 195 row 138);
    - the Spin2 operator: "?? (pre) ??var - Iterate long var per XORO32,
      return pseudo-random value" (spin2-v55-text.txt:412);
    - the interpreter, which implements ??var as the two instructions
      "xoro32 x" / "mov v,x" (Spin2_interpreter.spin2:319-320): x is the
      long read from the variable, v receives the XORO32 result, x (the
      iterated state) is written back, v is the value ??var returns;
    - SD:1183 (silicon-doc-text.txt) "XORO32 executes - Q is set to the
      XORO32 result", and SD:69 lists "XORO32 improved" (a revision note,
      no algorithm).
  An upstream lead (external-inputs/pnut_ts_facts/Random-Number-Usage-
  Guide.md:304-349, NOT a source) asserts "zero seed produces zero forever",
  but prints an xorshift that is not the xoroshiro32+ the Parallax documents
  name.  The KB must not state the zero case on that evidence.

  THIS PROGRAM MEASURES AND PREDICTS NOTHING ABOUT THE ZERO CASE.  It runs
  the same iteration three ways on the same seeds:
    P  a PASM cog: "xoro32 x" / "mov r,x" (the interpreter's own pair)
    L  a Spin2 cog: r := ??x with x a method LOCAL variable
    V  a Spin2 cog: r := ??x with x an object VAR variable
  for four seeds, 8 results each, the iterated state after each result,
  8 repetitions of every case.  No documented numeric result of XORO32
  exists (DS:1557 documents the instruction by name only), so the CONTROLS
  are CONSISTENCY controls: for a non-zero seed the three paths must agree
  exactly, be deterministic over the 8 repetitions, and the PRNG must move
  (the state changes, the results are not all equal).  They gate the rig:
  a failure prints RIG FAIL and NO VERDICT.

  SEEDS
    0            the question (zero seed)
    1            control seed (the brief's control)
    $DEADBEEF    control seed with both halves non-zero
    $0001_0000   half-zero seed (state bits [15:0] = 0, [31:16] = 1) -
                 characterisation: gated for agreement only, no reading

  ONE RUN (seed s, repetition r), on each path
    MARKER   a second variable m = MK_BASE + s * 16 + r (non-zero, a
             different seed for every run) is iterated once; its result and
             state are recorded (F_MKRES, F_MKST).  All three paths must
             record the SAME marker result for the same (s, r): proves the
             pair "xoro32 / mov" is correctly formed on every path in every
             repetition and that a result is not stale.
    CASE     x := seed; eight times: r_k := ??x; record r_k and the state x.
    The case's first result is compared with the marker's result and the
    count "equal to the marker" is PRINTED for information only; it is not
    gated.  Staleness is covered by two gates: the record tag (a record never
    written shows a wrong tag) and the marker gate (the marker is a different
    non-zero seed in every run and must be identical on P, L and V).
  RECORD (19 longs): tag, marker result, marker state, results 0..7,
    states 0..7 (the state after result k).  The tag
    (TAG_BASE + s * 16 + r) is written in the same block; a record never
    written shows a wrong tag.

RIG
  Bare P2 board, 200 MHz.  NO PINS, no jumper, nothing attached.
  Cog 0 (Spin2, the only cog with the debugger, DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001)
  starts the PASM cog (COGINIT, cog execution: no debug interrupt, no
  debug(), no BRK, and no interrupt is set up in it, so no interrupt can fall
  between a XORO32 and the instruction after it; SD:2349 also lists XORO32
  among the instructions that must not be executing when an interrupt branch
  happens), waits for it (1 s timeout), then starts a Spin2 cog
  (cogspin) that runs the L and V cases (no debug() in it), waits (1 s
  timeout).  The cogs run one after the other, never concurrently: there is
  no race.  Cog 0 checks and prints everything.  A cog that does not finish
  within 1 s is stopped and named (STALLED), never waited for.

PRE-REGISTERED READINGS OF THE ZERO SEED (printed by the program BEFORE the
  run; none is predicted - "no source states it")
    ABSORBING        all 8 results are 0 and the state stays 0 after every
                     call, on all three paths and all 8 repetitions
    LEAVES ZERO      a non-zero result or state appears: the first call at
                     which it appears is printed
    PATHS DISAGREE   Spin2 ?? and PASM XORO32 differ at the zero seed
    RIG FAIL         a control or gate failed; no verdict is printed

CHECKS (each failure prints RIG FAIL)
  - the PASM cog and the Spin2 cog both finish within 1 s;
  - every record has its tag; every marker is identical on P, L and V;
  - every NON-ZERO seed: P, L and V identical in every field of every
    repetition; DETERMINISTIC (8 of 8 repetitions identical);
  - the seeds 1 and $DEADBEEF also MUST move: the state after the first
    result differs from the seed and there are at least two distinct results
    among the 8 (the half-zero seed $0001_0000 is not gated on moving: it is
    characterised, and its movement is printed).
  - The zero seed and its agreement/determinism are measured and printed;
    they are never a RIG FAIL.

DEVIATION FROM THE BRIEF
  The brief asks for four ??x calls per seed.  This program records EIGHT
  (the first four are the brief's; the state after the 4th is the brief's
  "x after") so that a state that leaves zero late is still seen.  The brief
  asks for the PASM XORO32 loop "for each seed on the measuring cog": it is
  run on a separate PASM cog while the Spin2 paths run in a Spin2 cog, so
  the interpreter and the PASM never share a cog.  Two storage kinds (L, V)
  are run because the interpreter reads and writes a local and an object
  variable through different paths.  The brief's second control seed
  ($DEADBEEF) and a half-zero seed were added.

DEBUGGER
  Every printed line is assembled in lineBuf from hub strings and numbers and
  sent by the ONE debug(zstr_(@lineBuf)) record in ln_out(); the only other
  record is debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION").  The listing reports the DEBUG record
  count and DEBUG data size (recorded below).

OPCODES AND ADDRESSES  (pnut-ts -d -l, v1.55.8, read from the .lst)
  The .lst is a hub-image dump plus a symbol table; the PASM cog's object
  offset = $80 + cog address * 4 (pasm = $80, seedTbl = $70).  Read from it:
  XORO32 is EEEE 1101011 000 DDDDDDDDD 001101000 (silicon-doc-text.txt:5406),
  i.e. $FD60_0000 | D << 9 | $068.  Cog registers: c_mkbase $35, c_tagbase
  $36, c_donev $37, c_tbl $38, c_rp $39, c_si $3A, c_rep $3B, c_t $3C, seedv
  $3D, pmk $3E, pst $3F, record block r_tag $40, r_mkres $41, r_mkst $42,
  r_a0..r_a7 $43..$4A, r_s0..r_s7 $4B..$52 (19 longs, contiguous).
  Mailbox longs: MB_TBL 0, MB_REC 1, MB_CUR 2, MB_DONE 3.
    $080  rdlong c_tbl,ptra[MB_TBL]   $FB04_7100
    $0B0  xoro32 pmk                  $FD60_7C68   (D = $3E)
    $0B4  mov r_mkres,pmk             $F600_823E   (the very next long: its S
                                                    is replaced by the result)
    $0B8  mov r_mkst,pmk              $F600_843E
    $0C0  xoro32 pst                  $FD60_7E68   (D = $3F)
    $0C4  mov r_a0,pst                $F600_863F   (the very next long)
    $0C8  mov r_s0,pst                $F600_963F
    ... the same xoro32 pst / mov r_aK,pst / mov r_sK,pst triple for K = 1..7
    $120  setq #18                    $FD64_2428   (RECW - 1 = 18)
    $124  wrlong r_tag,c_rp           $FC60_8039   (the 19-long block, tag first)
  The Spin2 cog (method run_local, object offset $1521; run_var, $155D; the
  offsets move with any edit of the Spin2 text above them - re-read them):
    r := ??m  (m a method local, index 5)   D5 2B F6   (D0 + n = local n
              reference; $2B = the ??var push bytecode as emitted; F0 + n =
              pop into local n)
    r := ??vm (vm an object VAR)            5C A0 3B 2B F4
    The bytecode number $2B is read from the listing; it is not decoded
    against the interpreter's table (the interpreter's ??var path is
    Spin2_interpreter.spin2:319-320, 'l: ??var (isolated)', 'm: ??var (push)').
  The listing reports 2 DEBUG records, 24 bytes of DEBUG data.
  If you edit this file, recompile with -l and re-read every row above.

HOW TO RUN
  USB serial must be connected (DEBUG rides P62/P63).  Compile with
  pnut-ts -d, load to RAM with DEBUG on (pnut-term-ts, or PNut Ctrl-F10).
  Runs once, in well under a second; nothing is written to flash.
  SAVE THE WHOLE CONSOLE OUTPUT - it is the only record.
  Expected run time: about 1 s at most (each cog is waited for at most 1 s).
  A run that prints no "=== END" line and no DEBUG_END_SESSION within 10 s is
  a hang or a lost session: report it as such, not as a reading.
  Clock: _clkfreq = 200 MHz assumes the board's 20 MHz crystal (the listing's
  CLKMODE is $010009FB, read from the .lst); the 1 s timeouts use clkfreq.
  Output: the header and pre-registered readings, one line per seed per path
  (plus a raw line for every repetition of a path that VARIES), the verdict
  lines (each with the zero seed's repeatability on P, L and V), the END line,
  then DEBUG_END_SESSION.
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq        = 200_000_000         ' system clock: 200 MHz
  DEBUG_COGS      = %0000_0001          ' debug interrupt in cog 0 ONLY

  REPS            = 8                   ' repetitions of every case
  NSEED           = 4                   ' seeds in seedTbl
  NITER           = 8                   ' results per run
  NPATH           = 3                   ' P (PASM), L (Spin2 local), V (Spin2 VAR)
  RECW            = 19                  ' longs per record: tag, mk res, mk state, 8 res, 8 state
  MK_BASE         = $0C0F_FEE1          ' marker seed = MK_BASE + seed * 16 + rep (never 0)
  RUN_SHIFT       = 4                   ' seed * 16 + rep
  TAG_BASE        = $5059_0000          ' record tag = TAG_BASE + seed * 16 + rep
  DONE_V          = $0D0E_0D0E          ' a cog is done
  UNWRITTEN       = $EEEE_EEEE          ' fill before a run
  CUR_REP_MASK    = $F
  CUR_SEED_MASK   = $F

  SEED_ZERO       = 0                   ' the question
  SEED_ONE        = 1
  SEED_DEAD       = $DEADBEEF
  SEED_HALF       = $0001_0000

  LINE_MAX        = 480                 ' longest printed line (chars)
  DEC_TOP         = 1_000_000_000
  DEC_DIGITS      = 10
  DEC_BASE        = 10
  HEX_DIGITS      = 8
  HEX_BITS        = 4
  HEX_GROUP       = 4
  HEX_LETTERS     = 10
  SPIN_STACK      = 64

CON ' ---- Identifiers ----
  ' paths
  #0, PATH_P, PATH_L, PATH_V
  ' Spin2 storage kinds
  #0, K_LOCAL, K_VAR
  ' record longs
  #0, F_TAG, F_MKRES, F_MKST
  F_RES           = 3                   ' results 0..7
  F_ST            = 11                  ' states 0..7
  ' mailbox longs (cog 0 <-> PASM cog)
  '  MB_TBL  - hub address of seedTbl     MB_REC  - hub address of the PASM records
  '  MB_CUR  - progress: seed * 16 + rep  MB_DONE - DONE_V once every run is done
  #0, MB_TBL, MB_REC, MB_CUR, MB_DONE, MB_LEN

VAR ' ---- Rig State ----
  long mbox[MB_LEN]
  long recs[NPATH * NSEED * REPS * RECW]  ' [path][seed][rep][field]
  long spinCur                          ' Spin2 progress: kind * 256 + seed * 16 + rep
  long spinDone                         ' DONE_V once every Spin2 run is done
  long spinStack[SPIN_STACK]
  long vx, vm                           ' the V path's variables (object VAR)
  long failCnt                          ' RIG FAIL lines printed
  long bPasmStall, bSpinStall
  byte lineBuf[LINE_MAX + 1]
  long linePos

PUB main() | pasmCog, spinCog, seedIdx
'' Run the PASM XORO32 cog and the Spin2 ?? cog on four seeds, check the
'' controls, report the zero seed.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local pasmCog - cog the PASM XORO32 cog started in
' @local spinCog - cog the Spin2 ?? cog started in
' @local seedIdx - seed index

  linePos := 0
  failCnt := 0
  bPasmStall := FALSE
  bSpinStall := FALSE
  print_header()

  longfill(@recs, UNWRITTEN, NPATH * NSEED * REPS * RECW)
  mbox[MB_TBL] := @seedTbl
  mbox[MB_REC] := @recs                 ' path P is the first block of recs
  mbox[MB_CUR] := UNWRITTEN
  mbox[MB_DONE] := 0
  pasmCog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @pasm, @mbox)
  if pasmCog < 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: coginit expected a free cog (0..7), got "))
    ln_d(pasmCog)
    ln_out()
    say(string("=== END: RIG FAIL (no PASM cog) ==="))
    finish()
  if not wait_done(@mbox[MB_DONE])
    bPasmStall := TRUE
    cogstop(pasmCog)
  ln_s(string("=== PASM cog "))
  ln_d(pasmCog)
  say(string(" ==="))

  spinCur := UNWRITTEN
  spinDone := 0
  spinCog := cogspin(NEWCOG, spin_worker(), @spinStack)
  if spinCog < 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: cogspin expected a free cog (0..7), got "))
    ln_d(spinCog)
    ln_out()
    say(string("=== END: RIG FAIL (no Spin2 cog) ==="))
    finish()
  if not wait_done(@spinDone)
    bSpinStall := TRUE
    cogstop(spinCog)
  ln_s(string("=== Spin2 cog "))
  ln_d(spinCog)
  say(string(" ==="))

  if bPasmStall
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: STALLED - the PASM cog did not finish within 1 s; progress long "))
    ln_h(mbox[MB_CUR])
    ln_s(string(" (seed * 16 + rep, or UNWRITTEN = never started)"))
    ln_out()
    failCnt++
  if bSpinStall
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: STALLED - the Spin2 cog did not finish within 1 s; progress long "))
    ln_h(spinCur)
    ln_s(string(" (kind * 256 + seed * 16 + rep, or UNWRITTEN = never started)"))
    ln_out()
    failCnt++

  repeat seedIdx from 0 to NSEED - 1
    report_seed(seedIdx)
  print_verdict()
  finish()

PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output.
'

  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' line output.  Text lives in hub (string(...)), not in DEBUG data: each line
' is built in lineBuf and sent by the single debug() record in ln_out().
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_c(ch)
' Append one character to the line (cut at LINE_MAX).
'
' @param ch - the character

  if linePos < LINE_MAX
    lineBuf[linePos++] := ch

PRI ln_s(pStr) | ch
' Append a zero-terminated hub string to the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

' Local Variables:
' @local ch - the character being copied

  repeat
    ch := byte[pStr++]
    if ch == 0
      quit
    ln_c(ch)

PRI ln_u(numVal) | divisor, digitVal, bStarted
' Append an unsigned decimal to the line.
'
' @param numVal - the number, read as unsigned

' Local Variables:
' @local divisor - the decimal place being printed
' @local digitVal - the digit at that place
' @local bStarted - a non-zero digit has been printed

  divisor := DEC_TOP
  bStarted := FALSE
  repeat DEC_DIGITS
    digitVal := numVal +/ divisor
    if digitVal <> 0 or bStarted or divisor == 1
      ln_c("0" + digitVal)
      bStarted := TRUE
    numVal := numVal +// divisor
    divisor /= DEC_BASE

PRI ln_d(numVal)
' Append a signed decimal to the line.
'
' @param numVal - the number, read as signed

  if numVal < 0
    ln_c("-")
    ln_u(-numVal)
  else
    ln_u(numVal)

PRI ln_h(numVal) | idx, nibble
' Append a long in hex as $XXXX_XXXX.
'
' @param numVal - the number

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - nibble index, 7 (top) .. 0
' @local nibble - the nibble value

  ln_c("$")
  repeat idx from HEX_DIGITS - 1 to 0
    nibble := (numVal >> (idx * HEX_BITS)) & $F
    if nibble < HEX_LETTERS
      ln_c("0" + nibble)
    else
      ln_c("A" + nibble - HEX_LETTERS)
    if idx == HEX_GROUP
      ln_c("_")

PRI ln_cnt(countVal)
' Append "n of 8".
'
' @param countVal - the count

  ln_d(countVal)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(REPS)

PRI ln_out()
' Send the line built so far as one debug() record and start a new line.
'

  lineBuf[linePos] := 0
  debug(zstr_(@lineBuf))
  linePos := 0

PRI say(pStr)
' Append a string and send the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

  ln_s(pStr)
  ln_out()

PRI rig_fail(pStr)
' Count one RIG FAIL and start its line; the caller appends the details and
' sends the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the text

  failCnt++
  ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
  ln_s(pStr)

PRI wait_done(pFlag) : bDone | startCt
' Wait up to 1 s for a cog to write DONE_V to its done long.
'
' @param pFlag - hub address of the done long
' @returns bDone - TRUE when DONE_V arrived in time

' Local Variables:
' @local startCt - CT when the wait began

  bDone := TRUE
  startCt := getct()
  repeat until long[pFlag] == DONE_V
    if getct() - startCt > clkfreq
      bDone := FALSE
      quit

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' header
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI print_header()
' Print the rig identity and the pre-registered readings, before any run.
'

  say(string("=== VO-S059: ??x with x = 0 - Spin2 ?? against PASM XORO32 (pnut-ts v1.55.8 -d, clk 200 MHz, no pins) ==="))
  say(string("Measured, not predicted: no ingested source gives the xoroshiro32+ recurrence, period or zero case (DS:1557 names the instruction only)."))
  say(string("Paths: P = PASM cog xoro32 x / mov r,x | L = Spin2 cog, r := ??x on a method LOCAL | V = Spin2 cog, r := ??x on an object VAR. 8 results and the state after each; 8 repetitions."))
  say(string("Marker before every run: m = $0C0F_FEE1 + seed*16 + rep iterated once; its result MUST be identical on P, L and V (else RIG FAIL)."))
  say(string("Controls (consistency, no documented value exists): seeds 1, $DEADBEEF, $0001_0000 MUST agree P = L = V in every field of every repetition; non-zero seeds MUST be DETERMINISTIC (8 of 8) and MUST move (state changes, >= 2 distinct results)."))
  say(string("PRE-REGISTERED READINGS of seed 0 (none predicted):"))
  say(string("  ABSORBING      = all 8 results 0 and the state 0 after every call, on P, L and V, in all 8 repetitions"))
  say(string("  LEAVES ZERO    = a non-zero result or state appears (the first call is printed)"))
  say(string("  PATHS DISAGREE = Spin2 ?? and PASM XORO32 differ at seed 0"))
  say(string("  (an upstream note says 'zero stays zero' - that is a lead, not a source; this run decides)"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' records
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI rec_idx(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, fieldIdx) : recIndex
' Index into recs of one field of one run.
'
' @param pathIdx - PATH_P, PATH_L, PATH_V
' @param seedIdx - seed index
' @param repIdx - repetition
' @param fieldIdx - record long
' @returns recIndex - index into recs

  recIndex := ((pathIdx * NSEED + seedIdx) * REPS + repIdx) * RECW + fieldIdx

PRI rec_at(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, fieldIdx) : fieldVal
' One field of one run.
'
' @param pathIdx - PATH_P, PATH_L, PATH_V
' @param seedIdx - seed index
' @param repIdx - repetition
' @param fieldIdx - record long
' @returns fieldVal - the recorded long

  fieldVal := recs[rec_idx(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, fieldIdx)]

PRI seed_of(seedIdx) : seedVal
' @param seedIdx - seed index
' @returns seedVal - the seed

  seedVal := long[@seedTbl][seedIdx]

PRI path_text(pathIdx) : pText
' @param pathIdx - path
' @returns pText - the path as printed

  pText := lookupz(pathIdx: string("P PASM xoro32 "), string("L Spin2 local "), string("V Spin2 VAR   "))

PRI run_same(pathA, pathB, seedIdx, repA, repB) : bSame | fieldIdx
' Whether two runs of one seed agree in every field except the tag.
'
' @param pathA - first path
' @param pathB - second path
' @param seedIdx - seed index
' @param repA - repetition of the first
' @param repB - repetition of the second
' @returns bSame - TRUE when the 8 results and 8 states (F_RES .. the last state) are all equal
'   The marker fields are NOT compared here: the marker seed differs per repetition by design
'   ($0C0F_FEE1 + seed*16 + rep), so including them made every cross-repetition comparison
'   fail (bench run 2026-10-09: 9 false RIG FAILs). Marker agreement across paths is checked
'   on its own in report_seed (mkAgreeCnt).

' Local Variables:
' @local fieldIdx - record long

  bSame := TRUE
  repeat fieldIdx from F_RES to RECW - 1
    if rec_at(pathA, seedIdx, repA, fieldIdx) <> rec_at(pathB, seedIdx, repB, fieldIdx)
      bSame := FALSE

PRI first_nz(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, baseField) : iterIdx | k
' The first iteration whose result (baseField = F_RES) or state
' (baseField = F_ST) is non-zero.
'
' @param pathIdx - path
' @param seedIdx - seed index
' @param repIdx - repetition
' @param baseField - F_RES or F_ST
' @returns iterIdx - 0..7, or -1 when all 8 are zero

' Local Variables:
' @local k - iteration

  iterIdx := -1
  repeat k from 0 to NITER - 1
    if rec_at(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, baseField + k) <> 0
      iterIdx := k
      quit

PRI distinct_results(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx) : distinctCnt | k, j, bSeen
' How many distinct values among the 8 results of a run.
'
' @param pathIdx - path
' @param seedIdx - seed index
' @param repIdx - repetition
' @returns distinctCnt - distinct results

' Local Variables:
' @local k - result index
' @local j - earlier result index
' @local bSeen - the result occurred earlier

  distinctCnt := 0
  repeat k from 0 to NITER - 1
    bSeen := FALSE
    if k > 0
      repeat j from 0 to k - 1
        if rec_at(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, F_RES + j) == rec_at(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, F_RES + k)
          bSeen := TRUE
    if not bSeen
      distinctCnt++

PRI ln_run(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx) | k
' Append one run: marker, 8 results, 8 states.
'
' @param pathIdx - path
' @param seedIdx - seed index
' @param repIdx - repetition

' Local Variables:
' @local k - iteration

  ln_s(string("mk "))
  ln_h(rec_at(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, F_MKRES))
  ln_c("/")
  ln_h(rec_at(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, F_MKST))
  ln_s(string(" | res"))
  repeat k from 0 to NITER - 1
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_h(rec_at(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, F_RES + k))
  ln_s(string(" | state"))
  repeat k from 0 to NITER - 1
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_h(rec_at(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, F_ST + k))

PRI report_seed(seedIdx) | pathIdx, repIdx, sameCnt, tagCnt, eqMkCnt, agreeCnt, mkAgreeCnt, bZeroSeed, bMove
' Check one seed's runs on the three paths, update the gates and print
' its lines.
'
' @param seedIdx - seed index

' Local Variables:
' @local pathIdx - path
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local sameCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0
' @local tagCnt - records whose tag is right
' @local eqMkCnt - repetitions whose first result equals the marker's result
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions identical to the PASM path's
' @local mkAgreeCnt - repetitions whose marker equals the PASM path's marker
' @local bZeroSeed - this is the zero seed
' @local bMove - the PRNG moved (state changed, >= 2 distinct results)

  bZeroSeed := seed_of(seedIdx) == SEED_ZERO
  ln_s(string("--- seed "))
  ln_h(seed_of(seedIdx))
  if bZeroSeed
    ln_s(string(" (THE QUESTION)"))
  say(string(" ---"))
  repeat pathIdx from PATH_P to PATH_V
    sameCnt := 0
    tagCnt := 0
    eqMkCnt := 0
    agreeCnt := 0
    mkAgreeCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      if run_same(pathIdx, pathIdx, seedIdx, 0, repIdx)
        sameCnt++
      if rec_at(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, F_TAG) == TAG_BASE + (seedIdx << RUN_SHIFT) + repIdx
        tagCnt++
      if rec_at(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, F_RES) == rec_at(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, F_MKRES)
        eqMkCnt++
      if run_same(PATH_P, pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, repIdx)
        agreeCnt++
      if rec_at(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, F_MKRES) == rec_at(PATH_P, seedIdx, repIdx, F_MKRES) and rec_at(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx, F_MKST) == rec_at(PATH_P, seedIdx, repIdx, F_MKST)
        mkAgreeCnt++
    ln_s(path_text(pathIdx))
    ln_run(pathIdx, seedIdx, 0)
    ln_out()
    ln_s(string("   "))
    ln_s(path_text(pathIdx))
    if sameCnt == REPS
      ln_s(string(" DETERMINISTIC (8 of 8 identical)"))
    else
      ln_s(string(" VARIES ("))
      ln_cnt(sameCnt)
      ln_s(string(" identical to rep 0)"))
    ln_s(string(" | first result equal to the marker's "))
    ln_cnt(eqMkCnt)
    ln_s(string(" | identical to P "))
    ln_cnt(agreeCnt)
    ln_s(string(" | marker identical to P "))
    ln_cnt(mkAgreeCnt)
    ln_s(string(" | tags right "))
    ln_cnt(tagCnt)
    ln_out()
    if sameCnt <> REPS
      repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
        ln_s(string("   raw rep "))
        ln_d(repIdx)
        ln_s(string(": "))
        ln_run(pathIdx, seedIdx, repIdx)
        ln_out()
    ' ---- gates (every seed) ----
    if tagCnt <> REPS
      rig_fail(string("seed "))
      ln_h(seed_of(seedIdx))
      ln_s(string(" path "))
      ln_s(path_text(pathIdx))
      ln_s(string(" records with the right tag "))
      ln_cnt(tagCnt)
      ln_out()
    if mkAgreeCnt <> REPS
      rig_fail(string("seed "))
      ln_h(seed_of(seedIdx))
      ln_s(string(" path "))
      ln_s(path_text(pathIdx))
      ln_s(string(" markers identical to P in "))
      ln_cnt(mkAgreeCnt)
      ln_s(string(" (MUST be 8 of 8)"))
      ln_out()
    ' ---- controls (non-zero seeds) ----
    if not bZeroSeed
      if sameCnt <> REPS
        rig_fail(string("non-zero seed "))
        ln_h(seed_of(seedIdx))
        ln_s(string(" path "))
        ln_s(path_text(pathIdx))
        ln_s(string(" is not DETERMINISTIC ("))
        ln_cnt(sameCnt)
        ln_s(string(" identical) - a seeded iteration MUST repeat exactly"))
        ln_out()
      if agreeCnt <> REPS
        rig_fail(string("non-zero seed "))
        ln_h(seed_of(seedIdx))
        ln_s(string(" path "))
        ln_s(path_text(pathIdx))
        ln_s(string(" identical to P in "))
        ln_cnt(agreeCnt)
        ln_s(string(" (MUST be 8 of 8: ??var = XORO32)"))
        ln_out()
      bMove := rec_at(pathIdx, seedIdx, 0, F_ST) <> seed_of(seedIdx) and distinct_results(pathIdx, seedIdx, 0) >= 2
      if not bMove and seed_of(seedIdx) <> SEED_HALF
        rig_fail(string("non-zero seed "))
        ln_h(seed_of(seedIdx))
        ln_s(string(" path "))
        ln_s(path_text(pathIdx))
        ln_s(string(" did not move (state after result 0 = seed, or < 2 distinct results)"))
        ln_out()

PRI print_verdict() | pathIdx, repIdx, nzCnt, firstRes, firstSt, agreeCnt, bAbsorb, bDisagree
' Print the zero seed's reading (seed index 0) when no gate failed.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local pathIdx - path
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local nzCnt - runs of this path with a non-zero result or state
' @local firstRes - first non-zero result iteration (repetition 0)
' @local firstSt - first non-zero state iteration (repetition 0)
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions of the zero seed identical to P (L and V summed)
' @local bAbsorb - every run of every path is all-zero
' @local bDisagree - L or V differs from P at the zero seed in some repetition

  ln_s(string("=== CONTROLS: "))
  if failCnt == 0
    say(string("all passed ==="))
  else
    ln_d(failCnt)
    say(string(" RIG FAIL line(s) above ==="))
    say(string("NO VERDICT: a control failed, the zero-seed result is not interpretable"))
    say(string("=== END ==="))
    return
  bAbsorb := TRUE
  bDisagree := FALSE
  repeat pathIdx from PATH_P to PATH_V
    nzCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      if first_nz(pathIdx, 0, repIdx, F_RES) >= 0 or first_nz(pathIdx, 0, repIdx, F_ST) >= 0
        nzCnt++
    firstRes := first_nz(pathIdx, 0, 0, F_RES)
    firstSt := first_nz(pathIdx, 0, 0, F_ST)
    ln_s(string("ZERO SEED "))
    ln_s(path_text(pathIdx))
    ln_s(string(": runs with a non-zero result or state "))
    ln_cnt(nzCnt)
    ln_s(string(" | rep 0 first non-zero result at call "))
    ln_d(firstRes)
    ln_s(string(", first non-zero state after call "))
    ln_d(firstSt)
    ln_s(string(" (-1 = never)"))
    ln_out()
    if nzCnt <> 0
      bAbsorb := FALSE
    agreeCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      if run_same(PATH_P, pathIdx, 0, repIdx, repIdx)
        agreeCnt++
    if agreeCnt <> REPS
      bDisagree := TRUE
  if bDisagree
    ln_s(string("VERDICT: PATHS DISAGREE - Spin2 ?? and PASM XORO32 differ at seed 0 (raw lines above are the finding)"))
  elseif bAbsorb
    ln_s(string("VERDICT: ABSORBING - at seed 0, ??x returned 0 eight times and x stayed 0, identically on PASM, Spin2 local and Spin2 VAR (8 of 8 repetitions)"))
  else
    ln_s(string("VERDICT: LEAVES ZERO - at seed 0 a non-zero result or state appeared (first call above); zero is NOT absorbing, the raw sequences above are the finding"))
  ln_zero_repeat()
  ln_out()
  say(string("=== END ==="))

PRI ln_zero_repeat() | pathIdx, repIdx, sameCnt
' Append the zero seed's repeatability on P, L and V: " | zero seed repeat: P
' DETERMINISTIC; L VARIES (n of 8 identical to rep 0); V ...".
'

' Local Variables:
' @local pathIdx - path
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local sameCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0

  ln_s(string(" | zero seed repeat:"))
  repeat pathIdx from PATH_P to PATH_V
    sameCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      if run_same(pathIdx, pathIdx, 0, 0, repIdx)
        sameCnt++
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_c(byte[path_text(pathIdx)])
    if sameCnt == REPS
      ln_s(string(" DETERMINISTIC"))
    else
      ln_s(string(" VARIES ("))
      ln_cnt(sameCnt)
      ln_s(string(" identical to rep 0)"))
    ln_c(";")

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' the Spin2 cog: the L and V paths
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI spin_worker() | seedIdx, repIdx, kind
' Spin2 cog: run every seed, 8 repetitions, on the local and the VAR path;
' write DONE_V at the end.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local seedIdx - seed index
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local kind - K_LOCAL or K_VAR

  repeat kind from K_LOCAL to K_VAR
    repeat seedIdx from 0 to NSEED - 1
      repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
        spinCur := (kind << 8) + (seedIdx << RUN_SHIFT) + repIdx
        if kind == K_LOCAL
          run_local(rec_idx(PATH_L, seedIdx, repIdx, 0), long[@seedTbl][seedIdx], MK_BASE + (seedIdx << RUN_SHIFT) + repIdx, TAG_BASE + (seedIdx << RUN_SHIFT) + repIdx)
        else
          run_var(rec_idx(PATH_V, seedIdx, repIdx, 0), long[@seedTbl][seedIdx], MK_BASE + (seedIdx << RUN_SHIFT) + repIdx, TAG_BASE + (seedIdx << RUN_SHIFT) + repIdx)
  spinDone := DONE_V

PRI run_local(baseIdx, seedVal, mkSeed, tagVal) | x, m, r, k
' One run with x and m as method LOCAL variables: marker, then 8 x ??x.
' The seed arrives as a parameter, so the compiler cannot fold it.
'
' @param baseIdx - index into recs of the record's first long
' @param seedVal - the seed
' @param mkSeed - the marker's seed
' @param tagVal - the record tag

' Local Variables:
' @local x - the case variable
' @local m - the marker variable
' @local r - a ?? result
' @local k - iteration

  m := mkSeed
  r := ??m
  recs[baseIdx + F_MKRES] := r
  recs[baseIdx + F_MKST] := m
  x := seedVal
  repeat k from 0 to NITER - 1
    r := ??x
    recs[baseIdx + F_RES + k] := r
    recs[baseIdx + F_ST + k] := x
  recs[baseIdx + F_TAG] := tagVal

PRI run_var(baseIdx, seedVal, mkSeed, tagVal) | r, k
' One run with x and m as object VAR variables: marker, then 8 x ??x.
'
' @param baseIdx - index into recs of the record's first long
' @param seedVal - the seed
' @param mkSeed - the marker's seed
' @param tagVal - the record tag

' Local Variables:
' @local r - a ?? result
' @local k - iteration

  vm := mkSeed
  r := ??vm
  recs[baseIdx + F_MKRES] := r
  recs[baseIdx + F_MKST] := vm
  vx := seedVal
  repeat k from 0 to NITER - 1
    r := ??vx
    recs[baseIdx + F_RES + k] := r
    recs[baseIdx + F_ST + k] := vx
  recs[baseIdx + F_TAG] := tagVal

DAT ' ---- Seeds ----
seedTbl         long    SEED_ZERO, SEED_ONE, SEED_DEAD, SEED_HALF

' ===========================================================================
' PASM COG (cog exec).  PTRA on entry = @mbox (from COGINIT).  No debug(), no
' BRK, no interrupt in this cog (DEBUG_COGS excludes it).  Each XORO32 is
' followed by the instruction whose S it replaces, as the Spin2 interpreter
' does (Spin2_interpreter.spin2:319-320).
' ===========================================================================
DAT             org     0        ' ---- PASM XORO32 Cog ----
pasm            rdlong  c_tbl, ptra[MB_TBL]             ' hub address of seedTbl
                rdlong  c_rp, ptra[MB_REC]              ' hub address of the P records
                mov     c_si, #0

seed_lp         rdlong  seedv, c_tbl                    ' this seed
                add     c_tbl, #4
                mov     c_rep, #0

rep_lp          mov     r_tag, c_si                     ' seed * 16 + rep
                shl     r_tag, #RUN_SHIFT
                add     r_tag, c_rep
                wrlong  r_tag, ptra[MB_CUR]             ' progress: the run about to start
                mov     pmk, c_mkbase
                add     pmk, r_tag                      ' marker seed (never 0)
                xoro32  pmk                             ' MARKER: iterate pmk ...
                mov     r_mkres, pmk                    ' ... S := the XORO32 result
                mov     r_mkst, pmk                     ' the iterated state
                mov     pst, seedv
                xoro32  pst                             ' CASE call 0
                mov     r_a0, pst
                mov     r_s0, pst
                xoro32  pst
                mov     r_a1, pst
                mov     r_s1, pst
                xoro32  pst
                mov     r_a2, pst
                mov     r_s2, pst
                xoro32  pst
                mov     r_a3, pst
                mov     r_s3, pst
                xoro32  pst
                mov     r_a4, pst
                mov     r_s4, pst
                xoro32  pst
                mov     r_a5, pst
                mov     r_s5, pst
                xoro32  pst
                mov     r_a6, pst
                mov     r_s6, pst
                xoro32  pst
                mov     r_a7, pst
                mov     r_s7, pst
                add     r_tag, c_tagbase
                setq    #RECW - 1
                wrlong  r_tag, c_rp                     ' the record, 19 longs, tag first
                add     c_rp, #RECW * 4
                add     c_rep, #1
                cmp     c_rep, #REPS                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #rep_lp
                add     c_si, #1
                cmp     c_si, #NSEED                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #seed_lp
                wrlong  c_donev, ptra[MB_DONE]
                cogid   c_t
                cogstop c_t

'--- cog data
c_mkbase        long    MK_BASE
c_tagbase       long    TAG_BASE
c_donev         long    DONE_V
c_tbl           long    0
c_rp            long    0
c_si            long    0
c_rep           long    0
c_t             long    0
seedv           long    0
pmk             long    0
pst             long    0
'--- the record, written as one 19-long block in this order (R_* order)
r_tag           long    0
r_mkres         long    0
r_mkst          long    0
r_a0            long    0
r_a1            long    0
r_a2            long    0
r_a3            long    0
r_a4            long    0
r_a5            long    0
r_a6            long    0
r_a7            long    0
r_s0            long    0
r_s1            long    0
r_s2            long    0
r_s3            long    0
r_s4            long    0
r_s5            long    0
r_s6            long    0
r_s7            long    0
pasm_end

